{
  "slug": "carrot-and-oat-cookies",
  "title": "Carrot and Oat Cookies",
  "blurb": "Soft, lightly spiced cookies packed with grated carrot, oats and raisins. A wholesome treat for any time of day.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat your oven to 180°C and line a baking tray with baking paper.",
    "Beat the softened butter and sugar together in a bowl until combined, then add the egg and mix well.",
    "Stir in the grated carrot, oats, flour, baking powder, cinnamon and salt until you have a thick mixture.",
    "Fold through the raisins and chopped walnuts.",
    "Spoon rounded tablespoons of the mixture onto the prepared tray, spacing them apart, and flatten each one slightly with the back of a spoon.",
    "Bake for 22 to 25 minutes until the edges are golden and the cookies are just firm to the touch.",
    "Leave to cool on the tray for a few minutes, then transfer to a wire rack to cool completely."
  ],
